From 2649bb17ee8a7c1b5713bed64a1f077af2fc5b49 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Viljo Marrandi <30616+vilts@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 15:29:26 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(import): state the STEP length unit, and ask for it
 when the file has none

A STEP model import now ends its notes with the length unit that the
model was read in: the file's own, or the unit that the caller stated.
A STEP file whose unit contexts state no length unit is no longer read
as millimetres. It is refused with ImportError::StepUnitsMissing until
the caller states mm or in:

- ImportModel::within_in / from_bytes_in, MCP import_model `units`,
  and the fourth argument of cam.import;
- the desktop app asks with a Length unit prompt (Millimeters, Inches,
  Cancel) and runs the same import again in the answer, as one
  undoable import. Cancel imports nothing.

The kernel writes the stated unit into the file's representation
contexts before the read (step_assumed_unit), so the tolerance, the
edge-gap cap and the chord stay in the unit of the geometry. A file
that states its own unit keeps it; the note names a caller's unit that
is not used. A unit for a mesh file is refused by name.

Fixes #1874

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
